    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The build passes with the test green. The audit log confirms the new identity in action: `customerCode=NSW-16E6609E` \u2014 region `NSW` (from postcode 2000) plus an 8-char upper-hex hash.\n\nHere's what I changed to move owner identity to `<REGION>-<HASH8>`:\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**\n- Replaced `nextCustomerCode(city, lastName)` (which counted per-city owners for the `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` sequence) with `buildCustomerCode(owner, normalizedTelephone)`, which builds `<REGION>-<HASH8>`: the region from `OwnerMapper.toRegion(owner)` and an 8-char upper-hex SHA-256 of `normalizedTelephone + lastName`. Added the `sha256Hex8` helper. The sequence logic is dropped entirely.\n- Updated the create call site and the stale capacity-check comment that referenced the removed sequence.\n- The create audit record already logged `customerCode`, so it now emits the new identity automatically.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`**\n- Extracted the region derivation (postcode-preferred, then city, else `UNKNOWN`) into `toRegion(Owner)`, shared by the customer code and locality.\n- Rewrote `toLocality` to derive from the `customerCode` \u2014 it returns the `REGION` prefix (before the first `-`), falling back to `toRegion` when no code is present. Locality now shares the region-and-hash identity rather than computing independently.\n- `toMembershipNumber` and `toCheckDigit` already read `customerCode`, so they automatically build on the new value (Luhn now runs over the hex digits in `HASH8`); updated the doc example.\n\n**Docs:** updated the `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, and `locality` descriptions/examples in `openapi.yml`. Existing DB `customer_code` columns (VARCHAR(20)/TEXT) already accommodate the max 16-char code, so no schema change was needed.",
